WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
Here's a strange first step for an analysis.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.680
Weigh out half a gram of dried potassium

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:06.600
sulfate.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.720
You already know how much sulfate is in

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.640
it, because you know its formula.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.440
So why analyse it?

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.080
To test your method.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.320
If it recovers all the sulfate you put

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.160
in, you can trust it on a real

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:18.880
sample.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.440
If not, you'll see how much it loses.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:27.066
The question: does digesting the precipitate improve the

00:00:27.147 --> 00:00:28.426
recovery of sulfate?

00:00:28.987 --> 00:00:31.386
Recovery is the mass of barium sulfate you

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.626
collect, as a percentage of the mass you

00:00:33.707 --> 00:00:34.346
should get.

00:00:34.907 --> 00:00:38.506
The independent variable is digestion: one set keeps

00:00:38.547 --> 00:00:40.906
the precipitate warm for thirty minutes, the other

00:00:40.987 --> 00:00:41.466
doesn't.

00:00:42.027 --> 00:00:44.186
The dependent variable is the recovery.

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:46.426
Everything else stays the same.

00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:50.553
First, the mass you should get.

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:54.273
Point five zero zero grams of potassium sulfate,

00:00:54.394 --> 00:00:56.673
over its molar mass, is two point eight

00:00:56.794 --> 00:00:59.313
seven times ten to the minus three moles.

00:00:59.874 --> 00:01:02.593
There's one sulfate per formula unit, and one

00:01:02.754 --> 00:01:06.433
barium sulfate per sulfate, so multiply by barium

00:01:06.514 --> 00:01:07.793
sulfate's molar mass.

00:01:08.274 --> 00:01:11.473
That's the target: point six seven zero grams.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.980
Dissolve the potassium sulfate in about a hundred

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.020
and fifty millilitres of distilled water, add a

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.660
little dilute hydrochloric acid, as you would for

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.060
a real sample, and heat it until it's

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.260
nearly boiling.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:29.180
Slowly add twenty millilitres of barium chloride solution,

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:29.820
stirring.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.860
That's more barium than the sulfate needs, so

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:33.900
it's in excess.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.940
Once the solid settles, a drop more into

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.100
the clear liquid on top should give no

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.140
new cloudiness.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.700
Then the precipitation is complete.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.060
Now the sets split.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.380
Set A isn't digested.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.900
Set B digests first, just below boiling under

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:54.060
a watch glass, for about thirty minutes.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:57.820
Then both cool to room temperature before filtering.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.940
You'd predict bigger crystals in set B, and

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.260
bigger crystals are less likely to slip through

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.300
the filter paper.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.780
Both sets filter through a fine paper that's

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:10.620
already been dried and weighed.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.340
Rinse all the solid out of the beaker,

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.420
and wash it with warm distilled water.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.420
How do you know it's washed enough?

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.980
Add silver nitrate to a few drops of

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:20.780
the washings.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.540
White cloudiness means chloride is still coming through,

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.100
so keep washing until the test stays clear.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.740
Then look at the liquid that ran through.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.900
Set A's filtrate is faintly cloudy.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.700
Set B's is clear.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.780
Dry each paper at about a hundred and

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.740
ten degrees, cool it in a desiccator, and

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.980
weigh it on the tared watch glass until

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:45.980
two weighings in a row agree.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.040
Three trials in each set.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.640
Set A's mean is point six three two

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.600
grams, and set B's is point six six

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:56.560
four.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.280
Divide set B's mean by the target, point

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.320
six seven zero, and times by a hundred:

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.320
about ninety nine percent.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.440
Set A recovered only about ninety four percent.

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:10.186
Reliable?

00:03:10.587 --> 00:03:13.306
Within each set, the trials agree within about

00:03:13.387 --> 00:03:15.466
a hundredth of a gram, and the gap

00:03:15.547 --> 00:03:17.866
between the sets is about three times that

00:03:17.947 --> 00:03:18.346
spread.

00:03:18.827 --> 00:03:19.626
Accurate?

00:03:19.867 --> 00:03:22.426
You know the true value, so recovery tells

00:03:22.507 --> 00:03:23.226
you directly.

00:03:23.707 --> 00:03:25.146
Set B is close.

00:03:25.547 --> 00:03:27.706
Set A is about six percent low in

00:03:27.867 --> 00:03:31.546
every trial, and its cloudy filtrate shows why:

00:03:31.627 --> 00:03:33.546
fine crystals went through the paper.

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:36.186
Repeats won't bring those crystals back.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.720
Is the comparison valid?

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:43.080
Only digestion changed, so the difference can be

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.600
put down to digestion.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.960
And the method measures only sulfate: the acid

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.240
stops barium carbonate forming, clear washings show the

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.520
barium chloride solution has gone, and constant mass

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.960
shows the water has gone.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.560
One more condition: the potassium sulfate must be

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.440
pure and dry, or point six seven zero

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.640
grams isn't the true value.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.240
So here, digestion improved recovery, under these conditions.

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:12.586
Now the risks.

00:04:12.867 --> 00:04:15.986
Barium sulfate barely dissolves, which is why it's

00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:17.906
swallowed for some X-ray scans.

00:04:18.387 --> 00:04:22.066
Dissolved barium chloride is different: it's toxic if

00:04:22.147 --> 00:04:25.186
swallowed, so your teacher prepares and dispenses it.

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:27.906
Wear gloves and glasses, and wash your hands

00:04:27.987 --> 00:04:28.626
afterwards.

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:32.226
The dilute acid irritates eyes and skin, and

00:04:32.307 --> 00:04:35.506
silver nitrate stains skin and harms waterways.

00:04:35.987 --> 00:04:37.946
Use tongs for the hot beaker and the

00:04:37.987 --> 00:04:38.386
oven.

00:04:38.867 --> 00:04:42.066
The filtrate and washings still hold dissolved barium,

00:04:42.147 --> 00:04:44.626
so they go into heavy-metal waste, never the

00:04:44.707 --> 00:04:45.266
sink.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.000
One line to keep.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:57.200
Recovery is found over expected, times a hundred.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.760
Under a hundred, something was lost.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.720
Over a hundred, something extra was weighed.

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:05.653
Your turn.

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:08.413
To check a method, a student dissolves point

00:05:08.494 --> 00:05:11.773
three five zero grams of dry sodium sulfate,

00:05:11.854 --> 00:05:14.333
and collects point five six one grams of

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:15.453
barium sulfate.

00:05:16.094 --> 00:05:18.813
Calculate the percentage recovery, and state what it

00:05:18.894 --> 00:05:20.533
suggests about the method.

00:05:20.814 --> 00:05:22.093
Pause here to answer.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.940
Point three five zero over one hundred and

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:39.060
forty two point zero four gives the moles,

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:41.220
and one to one, the same moles of

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.740
barium sulfate.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.820
So you should get point five seven five

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:46.180
grams.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.580
Point five six one over that is about

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:51.460
ninety seven and a half percent: close, but

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:55.220
slightly low, so a little sulfate is lost.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:58.100
The trap is dividing the two masses directly.

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:00.740
Last one.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:05.220
To test digestion, set C digests its precipitate

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.540
and washes it with three portions of warm

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:08.660
water.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:11.460
Set D doesn't digest, and washes it with

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:12.740
one portion.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:15.300
Set C's recovery is higher.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:18.420
Explain why this comparison isn't valid, and propose

00:06:18.473 --> 00:06:20.260
a change that fixes it.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:21.620
Pause here to answer.

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:36.393
Two things changed: digestion and washing.

00:06:36.754 --> 00:06:39.553
Less washing can leave dried-on impurities that add

00:06:39.714 --> 00:06:42.113
mass, so the difference can't be put down

00:06:42.154 --> 00:06:43.393
to digestion alone.

00:06:43.954 --> 00:06:46.193
Fix it by washing both sets the same

00:06:46.274 --> 00:06:48.753
way, until the washings stay clear with silver

00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:49.393
nitrate.

00:06:49.874 --> 00:06:51.953
The trap is just repeating each set.

00:06:52.354 --> 00:06:55.073
That helps reliability, but the washing would still

00:06:55.154 --> 00:06:56.033
be unequal.

00:06:58.034 --> 00:07:01.313
So, to trust a gravimetric analysis, test it

00:07:01.394 --> 00:07:03.993
first on a sample whose answer you know.

00:07:04.274 --> 00:07:09.073
Acidify, precipitate hot with excess barium, digest, wash

00:07:09.154 --> 00:07:11.713
until the washings test clear, and dry to

00:07:11.914 --> 00:07:13.153
constant mass.

00:07:13.354 --> 00:07:16.033
Then judge the recovery: close to a hundred

00:07:16.114 --> 00:07:18.753
means accurate, and a cloudy filtrate or a

00:07:18.807 --> 00:07:21.553
wet solid shows which way it's wrong.

00:07:21.634 --> 00:07:25.473
Next: precipitation titration and gravimetry practice.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:28.940
Here are the key notes.

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:31.100
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:31.980
to copy them.
